1. Recursion

Recursion is a programming technique in which a method calls itself repeatedly to solve a problem by breaking it into smaller subproblems.

Basic Structure
static void fun(int n) {
    if (condition) {
        return;
    }
    fun(n - 1);
}


4. Advantages of Recursion:

Makes some problems easier to understand.
Reduces the amount of code for certain problems.
Useful for tree and graph problems.
Useful for divide-and-conquer algorithms.
Essential for many backtracking problems.
